<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burgenland</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Burgenland is the easternmost and least populous state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, a narrow strip of land along the Hungarian border with its capital at Eisenstadt. For centuries part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>, the largely German-speaking region was assigned to Austria by the treaties of Saint-Germain and Trianon after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. It was handed over in 1921 after fighting with Hungarian irregulars, while the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sopron">Sopron</a> voted in a plebiscite to remain in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/burgenland.jpg" alt="Burgenland" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Burgenland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Carinthian Slovenes and the Croats and Hungarians of <b>Burgenland</b> received minority rights under the State Treaty of 1955, and the Roma and Sinti were recognised in 1994.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-austria">Republic of Austria · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>Agnes of Poitou, regent of the Holy Roman Empire for her son Henry IV, met King Andrew I of Hungary to negotiate the border in the area of <b>Burgenland</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/september-20">20 September in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The peace treaties of Saint-Germain and Trianon assigned German-speaking western Hungary, later called <b>Burgenland</b>, to Austria.</blockquote><a href="/state/banate-of-leitha">Banate of Leitha</a></li><li><blockquote>The federal constitution of 1920, drafted with the help of Hans Kelsen, created a federal parliamentary republic; with <b>Burgenland</b> added in 1921 and Vienna separated from Lower Austria in 1922, it had nine states.</blockquote><a href="/state/first-austrian-republic">First Austrian Republic</a></li></ul></section>
